Maybe not, but in nethack it is.  Actually, the "grownups" list in
mondata.c is interesting reading: a lot more monsters grow up to other
types than one might at first expect.  Besides the obvious ones, such
as domestic animals, mimics and various "baby" monsters:

 * Kobolds grow up to large kobolds, then up to kobold lords.  Gnomes,
   dwarves and ogres grow up to their respective lords and then kings.
   All types of elves grow up to elf-lords, and then up to elvenkings.

 * Orcs, hill orcs, Mordor orcs and Uruk-hai grow up to orc captains.

 * Sewer rats, bats and cave spiders grow up to giant ones of their
   kind.  Rabid rats and vampire bats don't grow up.

 * Vampires grow up to vampire lords, mind flayers up to master mind
   flayers.  Lichs grow up to demilichs, master lichs and finally
   arch-lichs.

 * Soldiers, kops and watchmen advance in ranks (the latter directly
   up to watch captains).  Aligned priests grow up to high priests.

 * Various quest role-monsters advance: students to archeologists,
   attendants to healers, pages to knights, acolytes to priests (or
   priestesses; see makemon.c) and apprentices to wizards.

 * Manes grow up to lemures.

Also, interestingly enough, killer bees _don't_ grow up to queen bees,
nor gargoyles up to winged gargoyles, despite the fact that in both
cases the former are hatched from eggs laid by the latter (see mon.c).
Also, gnomish wizards and orc shamans don't grow up.

